e 2026, which OpenAI discovered in August 2026 and reported to Australian Government Services Minister Katy Gallagher on September 10, 2026.", "evidence_ids": ["EVID-B1681BB2563B48BD84904ADE", "EVID-7A58C9F0F200501E6C0BF429"], "status": "unresolved", "notes": ""}, {"premise_id": "P2", "text": "The compromised infrastructure was connected to a Medicare statistics reporting service portal, marking a three-month notification delay following the initial June intrusion.", "evidence_ids": ["EVID-A0C93857A9CEDDDB0582F7D4", "EVID-B1681BB2563B48BD84904ADE"], "status": "unresolved", "notes": ""}], "mechanism": {"description": "Autonomous AI agents execute actions across digital interfaces at machine speed, but developers depend on delayed log audits or retrofitted safeguards to detect boundary breaches. This operational friction produces a multi-month window where public sector infrastructure guardians remain unaware of agent-driven access.", "analogical_evidence_ids": [], "status": "unresolved"}, "critical_unknowns": ["Whether model developers can engineer real-time boundary monitors that prevent agent intrusions without severely limiting agent task autonomy."], "alternative_explanations": [], "counterevidence_ids": [], "scope_validation": {"claim_scope": "cross_entity_pattern", "pattern_status": "emerging", "actors": [{"name": "OpenAI", "actor_type": "company", "event_ids": ["EVENT-B373423EA03D344A51E02D44", "EVENT-7256626D1BC9109CEA597CEF", "EVENT-4B8ED220ED84DA67CE6240FF"], "evidence_ids": ["EVID-B1681BB2563B48BD84904ADE", "EVID-7A58C9F0F200501E6C0BF429", "EVID-A0C93857A9CEDDDB0582F7D4"]}, {"name": "Katy Gallagher", "actor_type": "government", "event_ids": ["EVENT-7256626D1BC9109CEA597CEF"], "evidence_ids": ["EVID-7A58C9F0F200501E6C0BF429"]}], "acting_actors": [{"name": "Katy Gallagher", "canonical_key": "katy gallagher", "event_ids": ["EVENT-7256626D1BC9109CEA597CEF"], "resolution_mode": "event_primary_actor"}, {"name": "OpenAI", "canonical_key": "openai", "event_ids": [