 appoint a new AI adviser, without providing details Trump says he will appoint a new AI adviser, without providing details Reuters REUTERS/Evelyn Hockstein/File Photo WASHINGTON, Sept 19 (Reuters) - U.S. President Donald Trump said in a social media post on Saturday that he plans to appoint a new artificial intelligence adviser, known as an \"AI czar,\" and create an \"AI force,\" though he did not provide details about either initiative or how they would be implemented."}, {"diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "event_id": "EVENT-042051769454F1BCF2054C2E", "source_id": "SOURCE-50419A862D1E9782B95B8F0E", "admission_status": "considered", "admission_reasons": [], "resolved_primary_actor": "OpenAI", "entity_mentions_state": "present", "raw_actor_fields": {"primary_actor": null, "acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "organization": null, "organisation": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"mention": "OpenAI", "entity_type": "organization", "role": "actor", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}, {"mention": "Australia's Medicare statistics portal", "entity_type": "unknown", "role": "object", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}], "event_keys": ["claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_date_precision", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_resolved", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "OpenAI agents hacked an Australian government website in search of data OpenAI agents hacked an Australian government website in search of data Australia's leader said it was 'unacceptable' OpenAI took months to report the incident. OpenAI's artificial intelligence agents hacked an Australian government website and attempted to breach numerous other government and university websites. Speaking on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly in New York, Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese said an agent from the American AI lab \"infiltrated\" Australia's Medicare statistics portal and \"accessed both public and non-public files.\""}, {"diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "event_id": "EVENT-4C4DEBE3A2A06B27AB123C3D", "source_id": "SOURCE-50419A862D1E9782B95B8F0E", "admission_status": "considered", "admission_reasons": [], "resolved_primary_actor": "Anthony Albanese", "entity_mentions_state": "present", "raw_actor_fields": {"primary_actor": "Anthony Albanese", "acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "organization": null, "organisation": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"mention": "Anthony Albanese", "entity_type": "person", "role": "actor", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}, {"mention": "Sam Altman", "entity_type": "unknown", "role": "object", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}], "event_keys": ["actor_recovered_from", "claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "primary_actor", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "\"This situation is obviously unacceptable,\" Albanese said, adding that he had spoken with OpenAI CEO Sam Altman \"to express Australia's extreme concern.\""}, {"diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "event_id": "EVENT-5840687EFBBBE526533F203B", "source_id": "SOURCE-50419A862D1E9782B95B8F0E", "admission_status": "considered", "admission_reasons": [], "resolved_primary_actor": "OpenAI", "entity_mentions_state": "present", "raw_actor_fields": {"primary_actor": null, "acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "organization": null, "organisation": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"mention": "OpenAI", "entity_type": "organization", "role": "actor", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}, {"mention": "government", "entity_type": "unknown", "role": "object", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}], "event_keys": ["claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_date_precision", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_resolved", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "Despite the breach happening in June, Albanese said the tech giant only notified the government about the incident earlier this month and did so via an email to a generic \"public mailbox.\""}, {"diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "event_id": "EVENT-D7B2440E579DFBD39D35E5DE", "source_id": "SOURCE-50419A862D1E9782B95B8F0E", "admission_status": "considered", "admission_reasons": [], "resolved_primary_actor": "Transluce", "entity_mentions_state": "present", "raw_actor_fields": {"primary_actor": null, "acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "organization": null, "organisation": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"mention": "Transluce", "entity_type": "organization", "role": "actor", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}, {"mention": "websites linked to the University of New Mexico, the Australian Institute of Health and Welfare, and Data USA", "entity_type": "unknown", "role": "object", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}], "event_keys": ["claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_date_precision", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_resolved", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "Three further incidents of rogue AI activity linked to OpenAI agents were also reported on Wednesday by research lab Transluce. The group, which describes itself as a \"nonprofit research lab dedicated to public oversight\" of AI, said it had identified evidence that OpenAI's systems had attempted to compromise websites linked to the University of New Mexico, the Australian Institute of Health and Welfare, and Data USA, a non-government platform that aggregates data from US government sources."}, {"diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "event_id": "EVENT-0242507B013C85729657D3F8", "source_id": "SOURCE-522409DCAF21B3E9CFDA38B3", "admission_status": "considered", "admission_reasons": [], "resolved_primary_actor": "Commission", "entity_mentions_state": "present", "raw_actor_fields": {"primary_actor": null, "acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "organization": null, "organisation": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"mention": "Commission", "entity_type": "organization", "role": "actor", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}, {"mention": "model provider", "entity_type": "unknown", "role": "object", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}], "event_keys": ["claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_date_precision", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_resolved", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "The European Union has required them since August 2025, and since 2 August this year the Commission has been able to fine a model provider 3% of worldwide turnover. Article 55 of the AI Act has obliged providers of general-purpose models with systemic risk to run adversarial testing, assess risk at union level and report serious incidents without undue delay since August 2025. The penalties arrived in August. Since the second of that month the Commission has been able to fine a provider up to 3% of worldwide annual turnover or EUR 15M, whichever is higher. It can demand access to a model, order evaluations and require a provider to restrict its public availability."}, {"diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "event_id": "EVENT-10C50C86C45147D42A02257E", "source_id": "SOURCE-522409DCAF21B3E9CFDA38B3", "admission_status": "considered", "admission_reasons": [], "resolved_primary_actor": "OpenAI", "entity_mentions_state": "present", "raw_actor_fields": {"primary_actor": null, "acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "organization": null, "organisation": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"mention": "OpenAI", "entity_type": "organization", "role": "actor", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}], "event_keys": ["claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "The one thing that has happened is OpenAI filing an incident report about its own agents occupying a German wiki. A company reported itself."}, {"diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "event_id": "EVENT-A9E4E4DD07239AF02C5150DA", "source_id": "SOURCE-522409DCAF21B3E9CFDA38B3", "admission_status": "considered", "admission_reasons": [], "resolved_primary_actor": "Anthropic", "entity_mentions_state": "present", "raw_actor_fields": {"primary_actor": null, "acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "organization": null, "organisation": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"mention": "Anthropic", "entity_type": "organization", "role": "actor", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}, {"mention": "governments", "entity_type": "unknown", "role": "object", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"]}], "event_keys": ["claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_date_precision", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_resolved", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "Anthropic proposed a framework in June giving governments the power to block dangerous deployments , with penalties scaled to global revenue and thresholds set by training compute and AI spending."}, {"diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "event_id": "EVENT-62D5E5B338D312A58C3F0905", "source_id": "SOURCE-58036158F50E552381CC7C82", "admission_status": "considered", "admission_reasons": [], "